[ACT] (main) open a new tab; click query editor; type:
query {
  salesRepOrders(customerId: "{{org}}") {
    totalCount
    pageInfo { hasNextPage hasPreviousPage startCursor endCursor }
    items { id number createdDate status statusDisplayValue total currency itemsCount customerId customerName }
  }
}
[GQL] (main) execute (Ctrl+Enter)
[READ] (main) response panel via browser_snapshot

Assertions:
[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepOrders.totalCount >= 2 {DOC}
[DATA] items.0.createdDate >= items.1.createdDate (newest first, default createdDate:desc) {DOC}
[DATA] items.0.total > 0 {DOC}
[DATA] items.0.currency is non-empty {DOC}
[DATA] items.0.itemsCount > 0 {DOC}
[DATA] items.0.customerId = {{org}} {DOC}

[ERRORS] (page1) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (page1) pageInfo.hasNextPage = true {DOC}
[COUNT] (page1) items.length = 2 {DOC}
[DATA] (page2) items[] has no number overlap with (page1) items[] {DOC}
[ERRORS] (keyword) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (keyword) totalCount narrows to exactly 1 (the seeded Beacon order) and that item's number contains "SRO-ACME-KEYWORD" — {{ORDER_KEYWORD_TOKEN}} ('Beacon') matches the order's INDEXED CustomerName; NOTE the response customerName field returns the denormalized ORGANIZATION name (not the order's raw CustomerName), so assert on the narrowing + number, not on the customerName value (verified vcptcore-qa 2026-07-16) {DOC}

[ERRORS] (storeA) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (storeA) items[] excludes the {{STORE_ID_SECONDARY}} order even though it is newer {DOC}
[ERRORS] (allStores) errors[] empty {DOC}
[COUNT] (allStores) items.length > (storeA) items.length {DOC}

[ERRORS] (inactive) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (inactive) every items[].status is either "Cancelled" or "Failed" {DOC}
[DATA] (inactive) no items[].status = "New" {DOC}
[DATA] (inactive) totalCount equals the count of (baseline) items with status Cancelled or Failed {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] items[] includes at least one status = "New" AND at least one status = "Cancelled" {DOC}
[DATA] no items[].status = "Processing" (excluded — union of New + Inactive[Cancelled,Failed] only) {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] for the Cancelled order, items[].status = "Cancelled" (raw status preserved, not localized) {DOC}
[DATA] for that same order, items[].statusDisplayValue is non-empty and reflects the {{culture}} localization (differs from a raw enum dump, or matches the store's configured localized label) {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] items[] includes an entry with customerId = {{org_a}} AND an entry with customerId = {{org_b}} {DOC}
[DATA] items[] does NOT include any entry with customerId = {{unassigned_org}} (unassigned org excluded from the dashboard) {DOC}
[DATA] every items[].customerName is non-empty (denormalized name or member-lookup fallback) {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepOrderStatuses is non-empty {DOC}
[DATA] items include name = "New" {DOC}
[DATA] items include a composite status name = "Inactive" with a distinct, non-blank localizedName (e.g. a "Not active"-style label, not the raw enum) {DOC}
[DATA] "New"'s name is a value valid as input to salesRepOrders(statuses:[...]) per SR-GQL-030 {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepCustomers.totalCount >= 1 (the X-API still returns the rep's data — membership scoping is the only gate, per README §Settings) {DOC}
[DATA] items[] still contains organizationId = {{org}} {DOC}
